# CCTV Shop Website — Build Plan

Target location: `~/Projects/Internship/cctv-platform/`
Status: planning complete; awaiting switch to a build agent to scaffold.

The website's job is to turn a worried visitor into a booked site survey. It is a
trust/lead engine first and an online store second.

---

## Locked decisions

| Concern | Decision |
|---|---|
| Payments | None in MVP. Quotes accepted via a button; invoices are records only; deposit handled offline. Payment model stays in schema, unused, for later. |
| CRM / admin | Custom admin built into the same React app at /admin. |
| Messaging | WhatsApp click-to-chat deep links only (prefilled per page/category). Email via Resend for confirmations/reminders. |
| E-commerce | Deferred to Phase 5. |
| Customer portal auth | Email + password (argon2, JWT access + rotating refresh, email verification, password reset). |
| Hosting | Vercel (web + NestJS) + Neon Postgres. |
| API testing | Bruno (collections committed to the repo). |

---

## Tech stack

- Frontend: React 19 + TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind CSS v4
- Routing/data: React Router v7 + TanStack Query; Zustand for the quote basket + calculator
- Forms: React Hook Form + Zod (schemas shared with the API via packages/shared)
- Backend: NestJS (REST) + Prisma ORM
- Database: PostgreSQL on Neon
- Jobs/cron: Upstash QStash (delayed jobs) + Vercel Cron (daily sweeps)
- Files: Cloudflare R2 presigned uploads (browser -> R2 direct)
- Email: Resend
- Scheduling: Cal.com embed + Google Calendar sync
- Analytics: GA4 + GTM; server-side lead/source events
- Monorepo: pnpm workspaces + Turborepo
- CI/CD: GitHub Actions; migrations run in CI with DIRECT_URL

---

## Vercel constraint (NestJS as a serverless function)

1. No long-lived queue/worker -> use Upstash QStash for delayed jobs
   (3-/14-day lost-lead follow-ups, AMC reminders 30 days out) and Vercel Cron
   for daily sweeps (overdue-lead SLA, AMC expiry scan).
2. Prisma + Neon -> app uses the pooled DATABASE_URL with the
   @prisma/adapter-neon serverless driver; migrations run in CI with DIRECT_URL,
   never from Vercel.
3. Function limits -> presigned uploads go browser -> R2 directly; quote PDFs via
   pdf-lib (no headless Chrome); rate limiting via Upstash Ratelimit (not in-memory).

